{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואשלכם", :translit "va'ashlichem", :gloss "and I cast them"} {:he "חסר י'", :translit "chaser yod", :gloss "deficient yod"} {:he "שפרתו י' הדברות מהם", :translit "shaparto yod hadibrot mihem", :gloss "the yod was diminished from them — corresponding to the Ten Commandments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word ואשלכם spelled defective (without yod after ש), and the missing yod (=10) corresponds to the Ten Commandments inscribed on the tablets."} {:kind :gematria, :a "י'", :b "י' הדברות"}], :frame {:text "Moses cast down and shattered the two tablets of the covenant (Deuteronomy 9:17). The letters of the tablets were said to flee when Moses broke them; the acronym of אל תירא עבדי יעקב (Isaiah 44:2) parallels the letters of the Ten Commandments (Shabbat 105a–106a). The letters engraved on the tablets are described as הר הגבוה (Deuteronomy 9:21), and the tradition that the writing penetrated the full thickness of the stone appears in Shabbat 104a.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 9:17" "Shabbat 104a" "Shabbat 105a–106a" "Isaiah 44:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word ואשלכם spelled defective (without yod after ש), and the missing yod (=10) corresponds to the Ten Commandments inscribed on the tablets.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "י'", :a-value 10, :b "י' הדברות", :b-value 627, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:31.501310694Z", :model "glm-5.2"}